It's used for college admission in the&nbsp;
S.S and it's been around in some form&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:20.480
for nearly 100 years. In 2020 there were&nbsp;
over 2.2 million students who sat the exam,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:26.480
you don't need to be in America to take it. It&nbsp;
comes with its controversies and criticism and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:32.480
anything that's sat by that many students is&nbsp;
bound to have a cultural impact but the sat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:37.360
isn't like the extremely hard entrance&nbsp;
exams that we've seen from other countries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:43.520
like India and China, you don't even need to&nbsp;
know calculus to be able to ace the math section.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:49.920
It comes with a different motive, instead of&nbsp;
trying to rank what a student has already learned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:56.640
the SAT is supposed to be designed to assess&nbsp;
a student's readiness for college and it forms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:02.800
only part of a college application&nbsp;
alongside personal essays, references,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:05.600
school grades and extracurricular activities.

