This question uses trigonometry, you&nbsp;
just need to find the cosine of an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:08.320
angle and know that a similar triangle will have&nbsp;
similar angles. There's questions about parabolas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:13.760
circles and simultaneous equations.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.600
This is the section where you're allowed to use&nbsp;
a calculator but to be honest you don't need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:25.120
it for most of them. For a few of them though&nbsp;
